<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Library Management (PindahLibra)</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            A sophisticated bibliographic ecosystem that manages the lifecycle of physical 
            collections and digital resources with architectural precision.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Advanced Bibliographic Stewardship</h2>
        <p>
            Standardize your library operations with professional cataloging tools. PindahLibra 
            utilizes the Dewey Decimal classification system to organize the school's 
            entire collection, from academic textbooks and reference materials to 
            narrative fiction and periodicals. Librarians can manage book acquisitions, 
            digital resource links (E-books), and annual stock counts through a 
            unified administrative interface, ensuring that the catalog is always 
            accurate and up-to-date.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Barcode-Based Circulation & Fulfillment</h2>
        <p>
            Experience radical efficiency at the circulation desk. The system utilizes 
            barcode or QR-code identification for rapid student check-in and check-out. 
            Automated tracking of student borrowing history identifies active 
            readers and those with outstanding loans, while the 'Reservation' 
            workflow allows students to place holds on high-demand academic 
            titles.
        </p>
        <p>
            Overdue fine calculation is hard-wired into the student finance account, 
            ensuring that lost or unreturned materials are captured on termly fee 
            statements without manual intervention.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Literacy Analytics & Insights</h2>
        <p>
            Gain institutional insight into reading habits across the campus. Detailed 
            statistics per class—including total books borrowed and average reading 
            volume per student—provide academic leadership with the data needed to 
            evaluate and improve literacy programs. Identifying the most popular 
            titles and genres informs future resource procurement cycles, ensuring 
            that the library remains a relevant and vibrant center of learning.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

